A time plan lists each task with its starting time, working backwards from the time of serving. Start with the dish that cooks longest, prepare all raw foods first, and wash used utensils while food cooks.
**Advantages:**
1. the meal is ready and served on time;
2. all dishes are served hot together;
3. food is not overcooked or burnt;
4. fuel or electricity is not wasted;
5. the cook is less tired and less rushed;
6. the kitchen stays tidy and accidents are fewer;
7. time is left for other tasks.
Do not write only "it saves time": that repeats the question.
